# The root package-lock.json IS committed (it was generated from scratch, with no node_modules present, so it lists the optional
# native packages for every platform; a lockfile made on top of a Mac's node_modules pins only the Mac ones and breaks the Linux
# build with MODULE_NOT_FOUND). If you regenerate it, delete the old file and node_modules first, then run
# `npm install --package-lock-only`. Per-workspace lockfiles are not used.
careweave/*/package-lock.json


.vercel
